From: toph <tophswetel145@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: wps_nintendo_ie - Wii U pairing AP WPS IE under the Nintendo OUI

A real Wii U pairing AP sends its WPS attributes in a vendor element with the
Nintendo OUI (a4:c0:e1, type f4) and no WFA (00:50:f2:04) WPS element
(beacon capture: dvdhrm, "Wii U Gamepad Connection", 2013-03-23; drc-hostap's
own wpa_supplicant accepts WPS_DEV_OUI_NIN for exactly this AP). A real
GamePad in sync mode never approached a hostapd pairing AP that used the WFA
element.

New bss option wps_nintendo_ie=1 (CONFIG_TENDONIN builds): Beacon and Probe
Response WPS IEs use WPS_DEV_OUI_NIN and carry the attributes the way the
captured console does: WPS 1.0 (no WFA extension: no Version2, no
AuthorizedMACs), Config Methods and Selected Registrar Config Methods 0x0084,
in the console's order. The Beacon gets the same full set as the Probe
Response (the capture only shows the Probe Response; the pad scans passively).
Element layout follows the capture too: a4:c0:e1 f5 00 right before the WPS
element, no Supported Operating Classes or Extended Capabilities, and WMM after
the vendor elements. HT Capabilities/Operation are written as the console's bytes
(Greenfield, A-MPDU 0x19, RIFS) regardless of driver support. Independently of the option, a station's
WPS IE is also recognised under the Nintendo OUI (Probe Request, Association
Request).
